  "mutationRounds": [
    {
      "round": 1,
      "hypothesis": "INT4-gap-gated-expand2",
      "margin": -0.3973,
      "noiseFloor": 0.0594,
      "kept": false,
      "analysis": "Gap-gated expansion of the runner-up regressed the margin sharply (-0.3973 vs prev best -0.1422, well beyond noise 0.0594), indicating that expanding a near-tied #2 hypothesis dilutes the judged output rather than adding useful disclosure \u2014 the extra expansion likely injects competing framings that the joint judge penalizes as incoherence or hedging. The gating condition (~15% score gap) fires too often on advise rankings whose scores are naturally close, so the \"borderline only\" path became the common path and the cheap clear-win path rarely triggered."
    },
