  "round2Caveat": "Round 2 (INT5) hit the Fable 5 usage limit mid-run: webhook-verify arm + synth errored, so its margin is over 4/5 tasks. Round 0 (headline) and Round 1 are complete over all 5 tasks.",
  "finalMargin": -0.1422,
  "verdict": "v2: raw sgt beats the aot interleaving on uncontaminated tasks \u2014 honest negative; v1 verdict was rubric-leakage-inflated",
  "mechanism": "On uncontaminated tasks with symmetric cost accounting, raw sgt retrieval BEATS the aot-interleaved arm. The frontier model, handed raw sgt excerpts, already answers correctly and cites them (baseline correct~1, high quality/trace). The aot epistemic layer (route->advise->expand->judge->trace) adds real token + latency cost that the composite (0.25 efficiency weight) charges, and its added quality/trace does not exceed that cost when the baseline is already right. Both usage-strategy mutations (gap-gated 2nd expand; refute-retain) lost. Reconciles EXACTLY with run-002: aot is unrepaid wherever the baseline is already correct.",
  "whatWouldFlipIt": "A regime where raw sgt retrieval MISSES the right skill (aot route/advise/judge re-ranking surfaces it) or the disclosed excerpt would MISLEAD the base model (aot verification catches it). Good sgt retrieval + a frontier model on answerable tasks does not reach that regime. The sgt run one-shot cuts latency (timeEff, 0.10 weight) but not the disclosed-excerpt token cost, so it is ARGUED (not measured \u2014 the aot-with-sgt-run arm was not run) to be unable to flip a correctness-dominated composite.",
  "modelAndControlCaveat": "NOT a controlled before/after vs v1. v1 arms ran on Opus 4.8; v2 arms ran on Fable 5 (journal shows claude-fable-5; run hit the Fable usage limit in round 2). The task set also changed (3 -> 5 different tasks). So v2 is an INDEPENDENT clean negative on Fable 5 (-0.142), not a single-variable correction of v1. Three things differ (model, tasks, the two measurement fixes); the sign-reversal is not attributable to measurement alone. Why the negative is still robust: (a) the v1 flaws are demonstrable by inspection regardless of model \u2014 the reasoning-trace rubric literally contains aot vocabulary and the token accounting is asymmetric in code, so v1 +0.221 is untrustworthy on its face; (b) by the run-002 mechanism (aot helps when the base model is WRONG), a weaker model like Fable 5 should be MORE favorable to aot, yet aot still lost -0.142 \u2014 a stronger model would not be expected to reverse that in aot favor."
}